  "body": "Up until now the implementations have been relying on the platform's provided way of retrieving the name e.g. android: BluetoothDevice.getName(), osx [CBPeripheral name], etc.\n\nWe recently found out that BluetoothDevice.getName() is really slow. So I started thinking of how to implement our own name retrieval and wondering if that's something we should spec.\n\nThe spec simply [states](https://webbluetoothcg.github.io/web-bluetooth/#get-the-bluetoothdevice-representing):\n\n> 1. If device has a partial or complete Bluetooth Device Name, set result.name to that string.\n\nShould that be more specific? For example what name do we use if the device is advertising one name but generic access has a different name? Should we update the name after connecting to the device? If the user changes the name do we update BluetoothDevice's name?\n",
